WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
Four square tiles meet at a corner.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.490
Ninety degrees each, and no gap.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.870
Three regular hexagons
meet just as neatly.

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.060
One hundred and twenty degrees each.

5
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.140
Now try identical regular pentagons.

6
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.760
Round a point, a wedge-shaped
gap keeps appearing.

7
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:18.620
Why?

8
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.540
Is it the odd number of sides?

9
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.820
Or is something wrong at the corners?

10
00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.090
In this mission, you'll use the fact that
angles at a point sum to three hundred

11
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.590
and sixty degrees.

12
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.500
You'll find a polygon's angle sum by
splitting it into triangles from one corner.

13
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.170
And you'll get a regular polygon's
interior angle from its exterior angle:

14
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.400
three hundred and sixty
degrees divided by n.

15
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.620
Your mission: explain why tiles
can be squares or hexagons,

16
00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.880
but never regular pentagons.
